  data: {
    LLM: "Keep track of the number of cards you've captured. The 'Most Cards' bonus is often the tie-breaker in close games.\n\nThe 'Lillan' Trap: Because the 2 of Spades is worth 15 in hand, players often 'build' a 15 on the table using an Ace and a King, then wait to capture it with the Lillan for a point.\n\nDefensive Stalling: If you suspect your opponent has the Storan (10D), avoid leaving a combination of cards on the table that sums to 16 (e.g., 9 and 7).",
    Player: "Keep track of the number of cards you've captured. The 'Most Cards' bonus is often the tie-breaker in close games.\n\nThe 'Lillan' Trap: Because the 2 of Spades is worth 15 in hand, players often 'build' a 15 on the table using an Ace and a King, then wait to capture it with the Lillan for a point.\n\nDefensive Stalling: If you suspect your opponent has the Storan (10D), avoid leaving a combination of cards on the table that sums to 16 (e.g., 9 and 7).",
